The situation seems to be that u(x) (and also h(x)) tend to form kinks at certain points in the domain, after which no matter how low i make the tolerance(tested to some range), the tolerance does not decrease. The code has a way to ensure that the tolerance at each step does not exceed the tolerance at the previous step. This is maaged by setting the skip parameter (skp) to 0. 
I tried to reduce the tolerance and set skp to 1. While the tolerance fluctuated initially, there was a net overall decrease in the tolerance over time. However, after some iterations, the tolerance kept increasing agian. I have been tracking the energy and tolerance at each step in a file called output, and it seems like the enegy also increases when the tolerance is increasing. 

In my opinion the hessian is not enough to stabilize the system.

Show him the construction with the smooth transition regions. USe the fact that phi'' = (2m+1)(1-2t)^{2m}. Which for t \in [0,1] converges to 0 as m goes to infinity. Thus the hessian doesnt get much contribution.
